.TH POLAJUICE 1 "November 2026" "polajuice @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
polajuice \- photographic process emulator: cameras, film stocks, prints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polajuice apply
.I INPUT
.B \-c
.I CAMERA
.RB [ \-f
.IR FILM ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR OUTPUT ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B polajuice develop
.I INPUT
.RB [ \-o
.IR OUTPUT ]
.RB [ \-\-ev
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-linear ]
.br
.B polajuice serve
.RI [ DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-web
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B polajuice cameras
.br
.B polajuice describe
.I CAMERA
.br
.B polajuice films
.RI [ NAME ]
.br
.B polajuice inspect
.I INPUT
.br
.B polajuice paths
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B polajuice
renders a photograph the way a particular camera and film would have:
the optics (softness, vignette, halation, flash), the format (a square,
an instant print with its border, a Super 8 gate), the film's color
chemistry (a 3D LUT), its grain, the development (push, pull, cross
process), aging in storage, and optionally a print stock after the
negative. It is written in C17 with no dependencies and runs the same
pipeline in the terminal, in a browser page, and in the movie front-end
.BR superjuice (1).
.PP
A
.I look
is a
.I camera
(see
.BR "polajuice cameras" )
plus a
.I film
(a .cube LUT from the film library). Each camera has a canonical film
that is used when it is installed; a film of another process is refused
unless
.B \-\-any\-film
is given. Cameras with a sealed process (technicolor-3strip, autochrome,
polavision) take no film.
.PP
Input is JPEG, PNG, a 16-bit scene-linear PNG/TIFF
.RB ( \-\-linear ),
or a Nikon NEF / DNG raw, which is decoded through a scene-linear door:
the sensor's white sits a stop above display white and the top stop
rolls in through a shoulder, so halation and the film curve see real
highlights. Output format follows the extension: .jpg .jpeg .png .ppm.
.PP
Every JPEG
.B polajuice
writes carries its recipe (the whole look as key=value lines) and a
geometry line in the JPEG comment, so a render can be replayed, varied
or inspected later with
.B \-\-recipe
and
.BR inspect .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI apply " INPUT " \-c " CAMERA"
Render
.I INPUT
through the look. The default output is
.IR INPUT_CAMERA.ext
next to the input.
.TP
.BI develop " INPUT"
The straight print of a raw file: scene-linear decode, a stop up, the
scene shoulder, no camera and no film. For checking a raw, or as a
neutral base.
.TP
.BI serve " " [ DIR ]
Serve the workspace page on http://localhost:8000 with the native
engine rendering on every core.
.IR DIR 's
images (default: the working directory) appear in the strip; exports go
next to the source and looks are kept as
.IR DIR/looks/*.recipe .
The page itself comes from the installed web directory (see
.BR FILES ),
or from
.BR \-\-web " " \fIPATH\fR.
.TP
.B cameras
List the camera archetypes with their traits, admissible film
processes and canonical film.
.TP
.BI describe " CAMERA"
One camera in detail.
.TP
.BI films " " [ NAME ]
List the film library (and print stocks), optionally filtered by a
substring.
.TP
.BI inspect " INPUT"
Show what a file is: dimensions, the raw's model, crop and matrix, and
for a polajuice JPEG the recipe and geometry it carries.
.TP
.B paths
Print where the film library, print stocks and web page are found
(see
.BR FILES ),
flagging any that are missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS The look
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-camera " NAME"
Camera / format archetype. Required for
.BR apply .
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-film " NAME\fR|\fIFILE"
Film stock: a name searched in the film library (substring, case
insensitive) or a path to a .cube file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-film
Force the built-in scalar color engine.
.TP
.B \-\-any\-film
Bypass camera/film compatibility checks.
.TP
.BI \-\-print " NAME\fR|\fIFILE"
Print or scan stock .cube chained after the film (cinema
negative-to-print model). Shipped:
.IR synthetic_minilab ", " synthetic_cine_print ", " synthetic_archival_neutral .
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " PATH"
Output file; the extension picks the format.
.TP
.BI \-\-strength " N"
Blend strength 0..1 between the input and the look (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-develop " MODE"
.BR normal " (default), " push+\fIN\fR ", " pull\-\fIN\fR
with
.I N
in \-3..+4 stops in halves (push+1.5),
.B cross
(E-6 in C-41) or
.BR cross+\fIN\fR .
Not applicable to instant cameras.
.TP
.BI \-\-crop " MODE"
.B camera
(default): the camera's own format cut from the middle (square, instant
print, Super 8 gate).
.BR full :
keep the whole input frame at its own aspect; instant cameras then
border the whole picture.
.TP
.BI \-\-age " N"
Storage aging 0 (fresh) .. 1: fog, faded contrast, magenta drift.
.TP
.BI \-\-grain " MODEL"
.B classic
(default, overlaid) or
.BR silver :
grain formed from exposure inside the film, coarse in the shadows and
fine in the highlights.
.TP
.BI \-\-edge " N"
Development edge effects 0..2 (1 dilute developer, 2 stand
development). Not for instant cameras.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " INTEGER"
Deterministic grain seed.
.TP
.BI \-\-ev " N"
Exposure in stops, \-4..+4 (default 0).
.TP
.BI \-\-halation " N"
Scale the camera's halation 0..2 (0 off, default 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " NAME"
Lens contrast filter:
.BR yellow ", " orange ", " red ", " green ", " blue .
Orange on a black-and-white camera is the dramatic-sky classic.
.SS Scene adjustments
Applied to the light before the camera; 0 is off for all of them.
.TP
.BI \-\-temp " STOPS"
White balance warm(+)/cool(\-), \-2..2.
.TP
.BI \-\-tint " STOPS"
Magenta(+)/green(\-), \-1..1.
.TP
.BI \-\-black " LEVEL"
Black point: crush(+)/fog(\-), \-0.1..0.1.
.TP
.BI \-\-shadows " STOPS"
Lift(+)/drop(\-) the shadows, \-2..2.
.TP
.BI \-\-highlights " N"
Raw shoulder knee: softer(\-)/harder(+), \-1..1.
.TP
.BI \-\-contrast " N"
Scene contrast about middle gray, \-1..1.
.TP
.BI \-\-grad " STOPS"
Graduated ND density at the dark edge, 0..3;
.BI \-\-gradangle " DEG"
puts the dark edge (0 top, 90 right, 180 bottom, 270 left) and
.BI \-\-gradpos " OFFSET"
moves the transition, \-0.5..0.5 of the frame.
.SS Lens and framing
Applied to the input before everything else, in one resampling.
.TP
.BI \-\-denoise " N"
Chroma denoise 0..3.
.TP
.BI \-\-distortion " N"
Barrel(+)/pincushion(\-) correction, \-0.3..0.3.
.TP
.BI \-\-devignette " N"
Lift the corners, 0..2.
.TP
.BI \-\-rotate " DEG"
Straighten, \-15..15 (positive clockwise); the frame is trimmed to the
largest rectangle without empty corners.
.TP
.BI \-\-trimx " X" ", " \-\-trimy " Y" ", " \-\-trimw " W" ", " \-\-trimh " H"
Trim to a rectangle given as fractions of the frame (left, top, width,
height), 0..1 each.
.SS Recipes
.TP
.BI \-\-recipe " FILE"
Take the look from a recipe: a key=value file, or any JPEG polajuice
rendered. Flags given after it override it line by line.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-recipe " FILE"
Write the look used as a recipe file.
.TP
.B \-\-linear
Take a 16-bit PNG/TIFF as scene-linear (dcraw \-4 \-T, darktable linear
export).
.SH FILES
Assets are found in this order, the first existing directory winning:
.IP 1. 4
.BR $POLAJUICE_FILMS ", " $POLAJUICE_PRINTS ", " $POLAJUICE_WEB
\- each directory on its own;
.IP 2. 4
.BR $POLAJUICE_HOME/ { luts , prints , web }
\- one variable for a relocated set;
.IP 3. 4
.IR ./data/luts ", " ./data/prints ", " ./web
\- the source tree, when running from a checkout;
.IP 4. 4
.IR ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/polajuice/ { luts , prints , web }
\- what
.B make install
fills;
.IP 5. 4
the datadir baked in at build time (the Makefile's
.BR datadir ,
.I /usr/local/share/polajuice
for a system-wide install).
.PP
.B polajuice paths
shows the result. Looks saved from the page live in
.I looks/
under the served directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POLAJUICE_FILMS, POLAJUICE_PRINTS, POLAJUICE_WEB, POLAJUICE_HOME
See
.BR FILES .
.TP
.B POLAJUICE_THREADS
Number of render threads (default: all cores). The output is identical
for any thread count.
.TP
.B POLAJUICE_PROFILE
When set (and not 0), print render timings to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
A roll of Portra through a clean 35mm camera:
.PP
.nf
    polajuice apply photo.jpg \-c 35mm\-negative
.fi
.PP
A Polaroid that keeps the whole frame, a stop under, pushed two stops:
.PP
.nf
    polajuice apply photo.jpg \-c polaroid\-600 \-\-crop full \-\-ev \-1 \-\-develop push+2
.fi
.PP
A D610 raw, straightened and warmed, on HP5 with an orange filter:
.PP
.nf
    polajuice apply DSC_0042.NEF \-c bw\-35 \-\-rotate 1.5 \-\-temp 0.5 \-\-filter orange \-o hp5.jpg
.fi
.PP
Replay a render on another file, two stops of grad ND added:
.PP
.nf
    polajuice apply other.jpg \-\-recipe photo_35mm\-negative.jpg \-\-grad 2 \-\-gradangle 0
.fi
.PP
Work on a folder in the browser:
.PP
.nf
    polajuice serve ~/Pictures/cats
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error (unknown camera or film, incompatible
process, unreadable input, a value out of range).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR superjuice (1),
.BR super8ify (1).
.PP
Full documentation, recipe format and preset sources:
.I https://github.com/micomrkaic/polajuice
